    "result_text": "The sheet's due-total and overdue-total now leave out the single highest and the single lowest person's figure whenever three or more people have one. All 4 tests in `bin/e2e` pass.\n\n- **Server (`Rollup.java`)**: the TOTALS audit line's due-total and overdue-total now use a new `trimmedTotal`. It drops n/a values, sorts what's left, and removes the top and bottom figure if at least three remain. The claimed-total is unchanged. A TOTALS line is still written only when one of the three totals moves after trimming. For example, when Ben's due-total dropped from 2.00 to 1.50, the trimmed totals stayed the same, so no TOTALS line was written.\n- **Front end**: I added `trimmedSum` to `features/rates/rates.ts`. `features/header/totals.ts` now uses it for the sheet due-total and overdue-total, so the header, the rollup due-total and the overdue-total all show the trimmed figure.\n\nPer-person figures, per-grade and per-period totals, backing and the claimed total still add up every figure as before.",
